## Accepted technology direction — 2026-09-08 takeover

This accepted user decision supplements revision 2026-09-07-v2.4 without replacing unrelated requirements. Constitutional owner #170; evidence/proof governance #173; architecture proof #38. The accompanying ADR is delivered through the issue-linked takeover PR.

- **No Electron** for the Symbiote desktop application. Electron is excluded from eligible shell candidates.
- Rust owns `symbioted`, the canonical control plane, native Symbiote Agent Runtime, CLI, process/worktree supervision and first-party intelligence coordination. Strict TypeScript and preferably React build the workbench as compiled static frontend assets. Do not add Go as a second core language. Supported SDK/analyzer sidecars and protocol-based external extensions may use justified other languages.
- Tauri 2 is preferred, **not proven or finally selected**. #38 must test four or more concurrent agent streams, three active terminals with bounded scrollback, editor/diffs, integrated live Preview with floating chat/voice controls, project switching/restoration, cancellation/process-tree cleanup, crash recovery and reconnect. Exercise Wayland/X11, Windows and macOS as applicable, recording untested platforms explicitly.
- Prove WebView composition, focus, stacking, clipping, resizing, keyboard/IME, scaling, accessibility, DOM/source mapping and security. Preview including localhost is untrusted; it inherits neither workbench nor Host authority. An iframe is not the assumed security boundary. Require an isolated permission surface and narrow authenticated design bridge with validated operations. A failing hard requirement triggers an evidenced non-Electron alternative, not reduced Preview scope.
- Desktop is a Host client. Desktop and CLI share the native agent implementation; authorized headless work survives desktop exit/crash. Shared Rust libraries do not require one process. Isolate processes for trust, recovery, cancellation and resource limits without introducing a service for every concept.
- Extensions use versioned protocols; evaluate sandboxed WebAssembly for bounded suitable workloads. Arbitrary native libraries loaded into the trusted daemon are not the default plugin model.
- SurrealDB remains the preferred System Graph candidate pending actual-version, behavior, resource and deployment proof. Evaluate transactional control-plane persistence separately.
- Measure the entire process tree and attribute shell/renderers, Preview, language servers, database, analyzers, SDK bridges and agents. Require bounded queues/caches, backpressure, lazy loading, virtualization, real cancellation and project-service suspension. Blank-window measurements cannot prove workload efficiency.

These constraints preserve external-only, hybrid and native configurations, provider/authentication/billing separation, and Symbiote-owned completion. No shell, database, cross-platform behavior, benchmark or security boundary is certified by this amendment. Downstream implementation remains subject to explicit prerequisites and issue acceptance evidence.
